ADDITIONAL NOTICE FOR ROBOTIC USE

This software commands physical machinery. The hand-detection interlock it
provides is a convenience check built on a general-purpose vision model, not a
safety-rated protective device, and it is explicitly documented as such. It
misses hands. Anyone deploying this on a real robot cell is responsible for
providing an independent, safety-rated protective system (light curtains,
interlocked guarding, an emergency stop) that does not depend on this software
in any way. The "NO WARRANTY" paragraph above applies in full to injury and
property damage.
